{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430114-breaking-points-chart","id":430114,"title":"Breaking Points chart","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-06T05:57:32-08:00","id":430114,"title":"Breaking Points chart","content":"The Breaking Points chart displayed in the page 104 contains a number of redundant breaking points, perhaps a left over from where different levels carried different expectations?<br /> <br /> Consider, for example: Staying out of the Hisil for a week, or a month or a day carrying breaking points towards the Flesh. How does this works? Wouldn't sticking to the world of Flesh for a week carry on 7 breaking points before you hit the one for the whole week? same thing with a month?<br /> <br /> How about the clauses about the clauses concerning specific Harmony levels? you Hit Harmony 8 and that's immediately a breaking point towards spirit? likewise with breaking points towards flesh if you hit harmony 3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T06:19:36-08:00","id":430168,"title":"","content":"I think you're reading them in reverse, Staying in the Hisil for a week is a breaking point away from the flesh. Also, (I think, though I may definitely be wrong here) that you only roll for a breaking point after the first day/week/month.<br /> <br /> Those harmony levels got me at first too but this is a Layout issue. Everything below the &quot;Harmony levels&quot; only acts as a breaking point if you reach that level of Harmony. A werewolf with Harmony 3 can't eat processed food without risking slipping toward the flesh, but one at 5 LOVES him some taco bell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T06:35:44-08:00","id":430196,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Harmony X things are headings, not triggers.<br /> <br /> And really anything written below that is actually stuff the werewolf <i>wants</i> to be doing to get themselves back in order. Find yourself slipping to the spirit end? Go eat a burger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T06:41:50-08:00","id":430202,"title":"","content":"Yep, at least from the player's point of view... though I'd think the character would look at the burger the way we look at week old shrimp just before its changed out at the Wong's Casino on Mars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T06:57:47-08:00","id":430218,"title":"","content":"Thinking about it I don't really think &quot;Spending more than two days away from your pack.&quot; should be a breaking point toward spirit, and certainly not for harmony 8+. The way they've got it set up avoiding werewolves at high fleshiness will make you less fleshy, and do nothing at all at a point where that's actually a bad thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T07:53:19-08:00","id":430276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430114-breaking-points-chart?p=430168#post430168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're reading them in reverse, Staying in the Hisil for a week is a breaking point away from the flesh. Also, (I think, though I may definitely be wrong here) that you only roll for a breaking point after the first day/week/month.<br /> <br /> Those harmony levels got me at first too but this is a Layout issue. Everything below the &quot;Harmony levels&quot; only acts as a breaking point if you reach that level of Harmony. A werewolf with Harmony 3 can't eat processed food without risking slipping toward the flesh, but one at 5 LOVES him some taco bell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still not getting it. Those breaking points only apply when your harmony hits the extremes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T07:55:33-08:00","id":430277,"title":"","content":"There are supposed to be subsets of breaking points that only apply when you're at the extremes. It sounds like something went wrong in the layout and they didn't get broken out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T07:55:33-08:00","id":430278,"title":"","content":"Part of the point of a pack is to keep you grounded in the flesh. It's a large part of why the Wolf-Blooded and human members are so important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T07:57:16-08:00","id":430280,"title":"","content":"Yep, the more out of balance you are, the more things that can send you rolling back. It's actually quite helpful.<br /> <br /> ^I guess that makes sense, but it feels weird that avoiding them will either be a non-issue or <i>beneficial</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 03-06-2015, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T08:02:15-08:00","id":430284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/430114-breaking-points-chart?p=430277#post430277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are supposed to be subsets of breaking points that only apply when you're at the extremes. It sounds like something went wrong in the layout and they didn't get broken out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that chart doesn't specifies if it's extreme or not...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}